id: pm-3ig9b6
title: "Destination census rows cite terminal consolidation owners for five live commands, so the grammar gate certifies consolidations no open item will deliver"
description: "## Observed\nPM_COMMAND_DESTINATION_CONTRACTS in src/sdk/cli-contracts/grammar-contracts.ts carries consolidation rows whose named owner is a terminal item: assurance, config, profile and schema name pm-6apl (closed; it delivered the ops namespace and never touched these four), and history-author-acknowledge names pm-tqel (closed; it consolidated the history-* spellings and left this one at the root). init names the epic pm-n7rr rather than pm-npr3, the open item whose acceptance criteria decide the customization family. verifyPmCliGrammar and the command-grammar gate check that every live command has a destination row and that stale rows are removed; neither reads the owner's status, so a consolidation whose owner closed without delivering it is certified indefinitely.\n\n## Why it matters\nADR pm-pbyu rule 8 allows a live command to remain only under a target noun, a tracked consolidation owner, a package owner, or a reasoned keep-as-is exception. A closed owner is none of those. The census is the artifact agents and the surface ceiling rely on to know what still moves; five commands currently read as in-flight consolidations that no open item will deliver.\n\n## Non-goals\nDeciding where assurance and history-author-acknowledge land is the delivery task filed beside this issue; deciding init/config/schema/profile stays pm-npr3."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[6]: "area:sdk",cli,contracts,gate,governance,grammar
created_at: "2026-09-12T19:57:52.201Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-13T17:45:08.718Z"
