comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-12T19:57:54.472Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check: pm-yy8rmx (closed) filed the census and pm-wt43zj (closed) made it a gate; both check row existence and staleness, not owner liveness. pm-npr3 (open) owns the customization-family decision but the rows do not name it. No open item covers owner liveness of destination rows."
  "2026-09-12T20:04:30.266Z","harness:claude-code","Progress 2026-09-12: the second criterion is shipped (five rows repointed, fixture regenerated, contracts-snapshot --check and command-grammar gate green, destination_count unchanged at the same row count). The first and third criteria, the owner-liveness finding with its negative control, remain open and are this item's residual scope."
  "2026-09-13T16:06:34.343Z","harness:codex",Live all-status snapshot covered 2757 items with complete receipt. Owner-liveness enforcement also exposed completed item-files leaves and hot-path operations still labelled consolidation; classify the leaves as delivered and the six concise item operations as explicit ADR-backed exceptions. Register existing ctx/packages Commander aliases in the shared alias contract so compatibility is proven structurally. No synthetic dependency edges or duplicate items added.
  "2026-09-13T16:12:47.948Z","harness:codex","Operational observation: scheduled Auto Release run 34745705596 succeeded today and GitHub plus npm expose 2026.9.13; no duplicate release requested. Required live Sentry/telemetry gate passed with zero blocking recent Sentry issues, 2.19 percent telemetry finish error rate and zero failures missing error codes. This aggregate observation is separate from final command correlation and physical queue proof."
  "2026-09-13T16:18:39.003Z","harness:codex","Tracker validation inspected all 2426 closed items: history drift passed, while 170 historical items still lack some structured expected/actual/resolution fields. These are reported baseline warnings, not claimed repaired or backfilled with invented outcomes. Health returned ok with an integrity warning. The all-status assurance gates remain required for this tranche. Published 2026.9.13 verification independently passed npm metadata, npx/bunx CLI, MCP stdio, MCP HTTP, skills/apps and GitHub release checks on their first attempt."
  "2026-09-13T16:20:43.733Z","harness:codex","Repository-wide static quality passed: ESLint, duplication, contracts and generated surfaces, public/source/member docstring coverage gates, package boundaries, grammar, flag parity, refusal recovery, agent-token replay, tracker graph measurements, gate registry, SDK surface/import-cost, CLI transport floor, graph composition and record integrity. Dependency audit found zero vulnerabilities across all severities. Full source coverage now runs alone with four workers; no limits or exclusions changed."
  "2026-09-13T16:24:09.185Z","harness:codex","Fresh dependency disposition: registry-current CodSpeed still requires Vitest ^3.2 || ^4; typescript-eslint requires TypeScript >=4.8.4 <6.1.0; npm-package-arg 14 requires Node ^22.22.2 || ^24.15.0 || >=26 while pm supports >=22.18.0. Canonical open, unclaimed migration owners pm-fokyhh, pm-do5b, and pm-ksr40d were read in full. No compatible wanted update or known vulnerability remains; no peer override or runtime-support narrowing was introduced."
  "2026-09-13T16:32:30.127Z","harness:codex","All-status graph proof: 2757 nodes and 13746 deduplicated directed edges form one connected component with zero isolates or missing nodes. Execution graph is acyclic with 12 layers and critical path length 11; no active hierarchy cardinality or direction violations. Seven legacy hierarchy rows remain informational findings. Semantic-edge coverage is not universal (1505 nodes lack semantic edges); no artificial edges were added to inflate graph depth. The 170 missing closure records match the explicitly unrecoverable residual documented by completed recovery pm-e9zh, whose live close evidence and notes were read."
  "2026-09-13T16:36:48.414Z","harness:codex","Additional security/script checks passed: Trivy HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerability, secret and misconfiguration scan exited zero; ShellCheck style severity passed across every tracked shell script; repository tracked-file credential scanner and documentation-link gate passed. Typecheck passed for source, type fixtures, packages and examples. Hosted TruffleHog and PSScriptAnalyzer remain required PR checks."
  "2026-09-13T16:44:55.284Z","harness:codex","All 8815 tests passed in the full run, but exact coverage correctly rejected one untested owner-snapshot failure branch (99.99 percent lines/statements/branches, 100 functions). Added negative controls for missing item arrays, pagination, missing completeness, and unchecked completeness; each must reject certification. No thresholds, exclusions, or source behavior changed. Full 100/100/100/100 verification reruns after the focused controls."
  "2026-09-13T16:53:34.787Z","harness:codex","Token-surface diagnosis compared the candidate with a separately built unchanged main against the same tracker: full TOON grew from 1316746 to 1339308 bytes although semantic JSON growth was only about 5 KB. Optional exception reasons made the entire 218-row destination census lose tabular encoding. Normalize the full-discovery reason column to an empty string for non-exceptions while retaining real exception rationale, restoring uniform scalar rows without removing any contract or increasing the 1323656-byte ceiling."
  "2026-09-13T16:56:49.837Z","harness:codex","Uniform full-discovery rows measured 1322480 bytes, below the unchanged 1323656-byte ceiling; all 57 agent token surfaces pass. Added a real TOON encode/decode round-trip assertion for the complete destination table and retained assurance rationale. The prior in-flight coverage was stopped because source representation changed; final static quality and exact coverage now run sequentially against the settled source. Installed npm/Bun acceptance is refreshed from a newly packed artifact."
  "2026-09-13T17:15:21.862Z","harness:codex","Final local validation passed 8819 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 source coverage. Repository-wide static quality, linked regressions, typecheck, 57 token-surface budgets, Trivy, ShellCheck, secret scan and documentation links passed. Newly packed npm and Bun consumers passed real extension discovery/invocation, native/legacy author preview, item creation/comments/dependencies and npx/bunx acceptance. Implementation closure is prepared for the combined reviewed PR; this does not claim publication of these candidate changes."
  "2026-09-13T17:45:06.312Z","harness:codex","PR 1255 review evidence at 701ffaa6a6e8686d0f504d89d75925ced37d4dfe: all deterministic checks passed, including Windows after an unchanged-code rerun of an existing 30-second transport fixture timeout. DeepScan and CodeFactor report zero issues; strict branch protection was verified live. CodeRabbit completed a full review with no actionable code findings. Its separate 68.75 percent diff docstring warning names no missing functions: AST inspection confirms all ten changed named production functions have JSDoc; documented the one missing test harness and reran linked regressions plus build. All received bot artifacts and edited revisions were read, reacted to and substantively acknowledged. Greptile authenticated gate explicitly reports free review quota exhausted, and Sourcery reports weekly quota exhaustion; these are unavailable reviews, not approvals, governed by existing pm-e02lgu. The documentation/evidence follow-up will request reviewers again and wait for all final-head checks before merge."
  "2026-09-13T17:45:06.999Z","harness:codex","Fresh operational proof at 17:18 UTC: required production observability passed with zero blocking Sentry issues over the configured 14-day window, telemetry finish error rate 2.19 percent and zero missing error codes. Real contracts and history acknowledge preview probes each have one paired start/finish in one session at current backend timestamps; history retains its stable history-author-acknowledge operation identity. Both telemetry event and span queues were physically empty after flush. These observed aggregates and paired probes do not claim universal telemetry completeness; final post-merge queue and CI evidence remain separate checks."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-13T16:36:28.617Z","harness:codex","Delivery scope and graph semantics: this tranche joins package discovery, native history acknowledgment, and consolidation-owner verification under existing command grammar lineage. The complete graph remains connected and acyclic in execution order. Retained concise item operations are deliberate exceptions; alias provenance is not unfinished delivery. Broader customization placement remains pm-npr3, major dependency compatibility remains pm-fokyhh/pm-do5b/pm-ksr40d, and source docstring prose cleanup remains pm-dvwm. Historical resolution residual is explicitly documented in completed pm-e9zh. These independent areas are not claimed as delivered by this tranche."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-13T16:33:32.115Z","harness:codex","A command census must distinguish delivery status from provenance: retained aliases point to live canonical spellings, completed paths use completed dispositions, and only genuine pending consolidation rows require nonterminal owners. Check complete all-status ownership in one snapshot; fabricated graph edges do not prove delivery."
